<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: RUGBY UNION-WESTERN SAMOA SCORE FIVE TRIES TO BEAT IRELAND.</title>
<headline>RUGBY UNION-WESTERN SAMOA SCORE FIVE TRIES TO BEAT IRELAND.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Western Samoa beat Ireland 40-25 (halftime 25-12) in a rugby union international at Lansdowne Road on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Western Samoa - Tries: To'o Vaega 2, Afato So'oalo, George Leaupepe, Veli Patu. Penalties: Earl Va'a 3. Conversions: Earl Va'a 3</p>
<p>IRELAND - Try: Paul Wallace. Penalties: Simon Mason 6. Conversion: Simon Mason.</p>
<p>Attendance: 15,000</p>
</text>
